# SF116: review fixes for the limiter, the saved-settings readers, the bench serial tools, the servo peak, the LAN client start, the reconnect restart and the tool registration scope
#
# Intent: review fix, tests by name: motion_limit_core_test.c (a cable reading that stops arriving makes the limit hold after 3 s, and a first "out" reading must be stable for 2 s),
#   test_review_saved_settings_guard_precedes_nvs_open, test_review_serial_tools_schedule_and_bound_reply_wait, test_review_motion_peak_reads_are_shared_and_keep_first_step,
#   test_review_avatar_endpoint_requires_client_start, test_review_reconnect_stops_and_waits_without_deleting_task, test_review_allocator_scope_restores_at_depth_zero.
#   The start-up silence is unchanged on purpose: muted and quiet also silence status and error alerts; the safety cues use their own always-on paths.
# Placement: unit (body half).
# Upstream: none (MaiPai code only).
# Check after a flash: a plain proof (630 s) and the batch1 train; self.motion.status answers peak_dps with first_step_deg and a window id and keeps the peak after a read; no restart loop.
# Kconfig: none.
# Memory cost: none at rest (a few bytes of state; one mutex).

